1
00:00:00,298 --> 00:00:01,770
If your knee replacement
still

2
00:00:01,770 --> 00:00:03,570
feels tight two years
later

3
00:00:03,570 --> 00:00:05,917
and every X-ray comes back
perfect,

4
00:00:06,105 --> 00:00:07,378
there is one thing nobody

5
00:00:07,378 --> 00:00:08,662
in that room is checking.

6
00:00:08,900 --> 00:00:10,392
I found it the hard way,

7
00:00:10,550 --> 00:00:11,525
and it took my wife

8
00:00:11,525 --> 00:00:12,699
two years of her life.

9
00:00:13,096 --> 00:00:14,439
She is seventy-one.

10
00:00:14,916 --> 00:00:16,536
Worked outside her whole
life,

11
00:00:16,536 --> 00:00:18,208
never sat still a day.

12
00:00:18,545 --> 00:00:20,186
Then she had the knee
done,

13
00:00:20,186 --> 00:00:22,035
and she started moving
like

14
00:00:22,035 --> 00:00:23,437
a much older woman.

15
00:00:23,437 --> 00:00:25,267
The knee was tight from
the minute

16
00:00:25,267 --> 00:00:26,630
she stood up in the
morning.

17
00:00:26,918 --> 00:00:28,897
Like a band cinched around
it.

18
00:00:29,185 --> 00:00:30,716
By evening she was taking

19
00:00:30,716 --> 00:00:32,676
the stairs one at a time,

20
00:00:33,053 --> 00:00:34,476
both hands on the rail.

21
00:00:34,853 --> 00:00:35,927
And it woke her at two

22
00:00:35,927 --> 00:00:37,796
in the morning, every
night.

23
00:00:37,796 --> 00:00:38,224
I know,

24
00:00:38,224 --> 00:00:39,915
because I was lying right
there.

25
00:00:40,223 --> 00:00:41,177
She'd be up at two,

26
00:00:41,177 --> 00:00:42,053
then four,

27
00:00:42,291 --> 00:00:43,882
shifting the leg around

28
00:00:43,882 --> 00:00:45,125
trying to find a position

29
00:00:45,125 --> 00:00:46,308
that didn't ache.

30
00:00:46,308 --> 00:00:48,288
She wasn't tired from
doing too much.

31
00:00:48,526 --> 00:00:49,679
She was tired from a knee

32
00:00:49,679 --> 00:00:51,599
that never once let her
stay asleep.

33
00:00:51,906 --> 00:00:54,015
She stopped volunteering
to walk the dog.

34
00:00:54,184 --> 00:00:56,272
Stopped going to the
grandkids' games.

35
00:00:56,272 --> 00:00:58,171
Started doing the
parking-lot math before

36
00:00:58,171 --> 00:00:59,643
she'd even get out of the
car.

37
00:00:59,643 --> 00:01:01,145
So of course she went back
in.

38
00:01:01,751 --> 00:01:02,467
Over and over.

39
00:01:02,467 --> 00:01:03,421
Her surgeon.

40
00:01:03,421 --> 00:01:04,555
Her primary.

41
00:01:04,555 --> 00:01:06,494
Four sets of X-rays on
that knee.

42
00:01:06,494 --> 00:01:07,190
Scans.

43
00:01:07,190 --> 00:01:08,026
Bloodwork.

44
00:01:08,254 --> 00:01:09,606
An infection test.

45
00:01:09,606 --> 00:01:10,452
The whole list.

46
00:01:10,670 --> 00:01:11,854
And every single time,

47
00:01:11,854 --> 00:01:12,520
for two years,

48
00:01:12,520 --> 00:01:13,555
the same answers.

49
00:01:13,902 --> 00:01:15,453
"The replacement looks
great."

50
00:01:15,453 --> 00:01:16,428
"Alignment is good."

51
00:01:16,428 --> 00:01:18,625
"Probably just doing a
little too much."

52
00:01:18,625 --> 00:01:19,630
"Try more therapy."

53
00:01:19,630 --> 00:01:21,062
"Give it another six
months."

54
00:01:21,370 --> 00:01:23,120
She was already two years
out,

55
00:01:23,120 --> 00:01:24,273
and they handed her the
same

56
00:01:24,273 --> 00:01:25,368
six months again.

57
00:01:25,646 --> 00:01:26,242
Then they sent

58
00:01:26,242 --> 00:01:27,684
her for a nerve block.

59
00:01:27,684 --> 00:01:28,818
For about three weeks

60
00:01:28,818 --> 00:01:30,031
the knee went quiet.

61
00:01:30,031 --> 00:01:31,225
She thought that was it.

62
00:01:31,632 --> 00:01:33,064
Then it came back exactly

63
00:01:33,064 --> 00:01:33,989
the way it left.

64
00:01:34,346 --> 00:01:35,281
And the tightness

65
00:01:35,281 --> 00:01:36,833
never went anywhere at
all.

66
00:01:37,131 --> 00:01:39,100
That block quieted the
signal.

67
00:01:39,368 --> 00:01:41,298
It never touched the thing
sending it.

68
00:01:41,576 --> 00:01:43,197
That was the point I got
angry.

69
00:01:43,385 --> 00:01:44,907
I was watching a woman

70
00:01:44,907 --> 00:01:46,697
who did every exercise,

71
00:01:46,866 --> 00:01:48,457
went to every appointment,

72
00:01:48,457 --> 00:01:50,097
took everything they gave
her,

73
00:01:50,097 --> 00:01:51,371
and got no better.

74
00:01:51,609 --> 00:01:52,614
Not once.

75
00:01:52,782 --> 00:01:54,174
So I started reading.

76
00:01:54,174 --> 00:01:55,607
Not the surgical stuff.

77
00:01:55,815 --> 00:01:57,326
The tissue research.

78
00:01:57,326 --> 00:01:58,569
The work that never comes

79
00:01:58,569 --> 00:01:59,664
up at the appointment.

80
00:01:59,991 --> 00:02:01,165
And I found the thing
nobody had

81
00:02:01,165 --> 00:02:02,984
said to her in two full
years.

82
00:02:02,984 --> 00:02:03,900
They cut through it.

83
00:02:04,466 --> 00:02:05,570
To put the new joint in,

84
00:02:05,570 --> 00:02:06,912
they have to work through
the living

85
00:02:06,912 --> 00:02:08,593
tissue wrapped around the
knee.

86
00:02:08,593 --> 00:02:09,836
A sleeve of muscle,

87
00:02:09,836 --> 00:02:11,019
capsule and lining,

88
00:02:11,019 --> 00:02:12,412
packed tight around the
joint.

89
00:02:12,739 --> 00:02:13,773
All of it disturbed

90
00:02:13,773 --> 00:02:14,570
on the way in.

91
00:02:15,056 --> 00:02:17,563
Afterward, that tissue
swells.

92
00:02:17,900 --> 00:02:19,859
At first that's completely
normal.

93
00:02:19,859 --> 00:02:21,162
It's what tissue does.

94
00:02:21,162 --> 00:02:22,564
When it settles down,

95
00:02:22,564 --> 00:02:23,697
there's room again.

96
00:02:23,697 --> 00:02:24,652
The knee bends.

97
00:02:24,652 --> 00:02:25,964
Everything moves.

98
00:02:25,964 --> 00:02:26,909
But in some people

99
00:02:26,909 --> 00:02:28,481
it never fully settles.

100
00:02:28,818 --> 00:02:30,778
And swollen tissue takes
up room.

101
00:02:31,424 --> 00:02:33,164
Think about your foot
inside a shoe.

102
00:02:33,164 --> 00:02:34,944
The shoe never changed
size.

103
00:02:34,944 --> 00:02:35,730
Your foot did.

104
00:02:36,177 --> 00:02:38,364
Everything goes tight,
cramped, squeezed.

105
00:02:38,364 --> 00:02:39,538
Her implant was fine.

106
00:02:39,538 --> 00:02:40,572
Her problem was never

107
00:02:40,572 --> 00:02:42,144
the metal or the plastic.

108
00:02:42,511 --> 00:02:43,515
Her problem was that there

109
00:02:43,515 --> 00:02:44,839
was no room left in there.

110
00:02:45,007 --> 00:02:46,508
Bend it, and that swollen

111
00:02:46,508 --> 00:02:47,842
tissue gets compressed.

112
00:02:48,059 --> 00:02:49,830
Straighten it, and it
pulls tight.

113
00:02:50,068 --> 00:02:52,126
That is what the tightness
actually is.

114
00:02:52,126 --> 00:02:53,400
Not a part that failed.

115
00:02:53,727 --> 00:02:54,861
A room that got smaller

116
00:02:54,861 --> 00:02:55,955
while the joint inside

117
00:02:55,955 --> 00:02:57,507
it stayed the same size.

118
00:02:57,834 --> 00:02:59,405
And once you see that, you
understand

119
00:02:59,405 --> 00:03:01,047
why the nerve block didn't
hold.

120
00:03:01,324 --> 00:03:02,687
It turned down the alarm.

121
00:03:02,687 --> 00:03:04,427
The swelling doing the
squeezing was still

122
00:03:04,427 --> 00:03:05,999
sitting right where it
was.

123
00:03:06,276 --> 00:03:07,102
Here is the part

124
00:03:07,102 --> 00:03:08,405
that made my blood boil.

125
00:03:08,941 --> 00:03:10,373
None of this is a secret.

126
00:03:10,373 --> 00:03:11,508
It's in the research.

127
00:03:11,815 --> 00:03:13,207
But the appointment she
kept going

128
00:03:13,207 --> 00:03:15,107
to was built to answer one
question.

129
00:03:15,335 --> 00:03:16,857
Is the implant sound.

130
00:03:16,857 --> 00:03:18,816
And the answer was always
yes.

131
00:03:18,995 --> 00:03:20,795
A good X-ray ends the
appointment.

132
00:03:21,132 --> 00:03:22,635
It doesn't end the pain.

133
00:03:22,962 --> 00:03:24,474
There is no test for
tight.

134
00:03:24,712 --> 00:03:26,631
Nothing on that scan
measures how much

135
00:03:26,631 --> 00:03:27,786
room is left in there.

136
00:03:28,033 --> 00:03:29,137
So you can walk out

137
00:03:29,137 --> 00:03:31,087
with a perfect X-ray in
your hand

138
00:03:31,275 --> 00:03:32,548
and the exact same knee

139
00:03:32,548 --> 00:03:33,583
you walked in with.

140
00:03:33,870 --> 00:03:34,914
So I kept reading,

141
00:03:34,914 --> 00:03:36,704
looking for anything that
calms

142
00:03:36,704 --> 00:03:37,689
that tissue down

143
00:03:37,689 --> 00:03:38,734
instead of numbing it.

144
00:03:39,180 --> 00:03:41,071
It came down to four
things.

145
00:03:41,308 --> 00:03:43,258
660 nanometers.

146
00:03:43,585 --> 00:03:44,212
Red light,

147
00:03:44,212 --> 00:03:45,834
working nearer the
surface,

148
00:03:46,002 --> 00:03:47,971
where the tissue is most
irritated.

149
00:03:48,179 --> 00:03:49,920
850 nanometers.

150
00:03:50,427 --> 00:03:52,435
Near-infrared, reaching
deeper,

151
00:03:52,435 --> 00:03:53,847
down where the tissue
wraps

152
00:03:53,847 --> 00:03:55,071
around the joint itself.

153
00:03:55,399 --> 00:03:56,164
This is the one

154
00:03:56,164 --> 00:03:57,557
that matters most here.

155
00:03:57,785 --> 00:03:59,804
Both wavelengths running
together.

156
00:03:59,804 --> 00:04:01,883
Not one and then the
other.

157
00:04:02,180 --> 00:04:03,254
Both at once,

158
00:04:03,254 --> 00:04:04,389
the whole session.

159
00:04:04,696 --> 00:04:07,053
And twenty minutes,
sitting down.

160
00:04:07,053 --> 00:04:08,703
No stretching it farther,

161
00:04:08,703 --> 00:04:10,255
no pushing through
anything.

162
00:04:10,543 --> 00:04:11,309
You sit,

163
00:04:11,567 --> 00:04:12,920
and the light does the
work.

164
00:04:13,447 --> 00:04:14,968
In a randomized trial,

165
00:04:14,968 --> 00:04:16,400
people who had light
therapy

166
00:04:16,400 --> 00:04:17,474
after a knee replacement

167
00:04:17,474 --> 00:04:19,801
had less pain, less
swelling,

168
00:04:19,801 --> 00:04:21,263
and better early movement.

169
00:04:21,541 --> 00:04:23,022
It just isn't on the list

170
00:04:23,022 --> 00:04:24,753
of things that appointment
checks.

171
00:04:25,031 --> 00:04:26,523
So I talked her into
trying it.

172
00:04:26,940 --> 00:04:28,154
And here was the problem.

173
00:04:28,382 --> 00:04:29,446
The only place near us

174
00:04:29,446 --> 00:04:30,869
doing it was a clinic.

175
00:04:31,077 --> 00:04:32,628
Twenty minutes on a table,

176
00:04:32,628 --> 00:04:33,643
then drive home.

177
00:04:33,831 --> 00:04:35,273
Two hundred dollars a
session.

178
00:04:35,273 --> 00:04:36,587
Insurance covers none of
it.

179
00:04:36,864 --> 00:04:37,540
Booking it.

180
00:04:37,540 --> 00:04:38,257
Driving it.

181
00:04:38,584 --> 00:04:39,848
Sitting in the waiting
room.

182
00:04:40,394 --> 00:04:41,130
And the whole point

183
00:04:41,130 --> 00:04:42,453
of this is that you do

184
00:04:42,453 --> 00:04:43,895
it every single day.

185
00:04:44,292 --> 00:04:44,919
So I bought one

186
00:04:44,919 --> 00:04:46,112
for the house instead.

187
00:04:46,112 --> 00:04:47,177
Two of them, actually.

188
00:04:47,534 --> 00:04:49,494
Only her right knee was
replaced,

189
00:04:49,771 --> 00:04:51,402
but she'd favored that leg

190
00:04:51,402 --> 00:04:52,685
for two years,

191
00:04:52,893 --> 00:04:53,918
and the left one had

192
00:04:53,918 --> 00:04:55,578
been carrying the
difference.

193
00:04:55,578 --> 00:04:57,050
It's called the KenRelief

194
00:04:57,050 --> 00:04:58,771
Red Light Therapy Wrap.

195
00:04:59,078 --> 00:05:00,670
It straps around the
joint,

196
00:05:00,938 --> 00:05:02,986
so the light sits flat
against

197
00:05:02,986 --> 00:05:04,519
the skin the whole
session,

198
00:05:04,846 --> 00:05:06,715
instead of a panel across
the room

199
00:05:06,715 --> 00:05:08,436
or a wand you have to
hold.

200
00:05:08,853 --> 00:05:10,514
Both wavelengths together,

201
00:05:10,514 --> 00:05:13,238
660 and 850.

202
00:05:13,238 --> 00:05:14,880
Two hundred forty lights.

203
00:05:15,177 --> 00:05:16,729
And when I dug into who
they

204
00:05:16,729 --> 00:05:18,509
built it for, it was
people

205
00:05:18,509 --> 00:05:20,518
who had already had the
replacement.

206
00:05:20,865 --> 00:05:22,049
Not arthritis.

207
00:05:22,446 --> 00:05:24,416
Not sore muscles after the
gym.

208
00:05:24,634 --> 00:05:25,956
The knee that got replaced

209
00:05:25,956 --> 00:05:27,429
and stayed tight anyway.

210
00:05:27,607 --> 00:05:29,178
She used it every night,

211
00:05:29,178 --> 00:05:30,203
in her chair.

212
00:05:30,431 --> 00:05:32,072
After about three weeks,

213
00:05:32,072 --> 00:05:34,002
the tightness started
letting go.

214
00:05:34,359 --> 00:05:35,045
After a month,

215
00:05:35,045 --> 00:05:36,189
she was taking the stairs

216
00:05:36,189 --> 00:05:37,442
without the handrail.

217
00:05:37,690 --> 00:05:39,898
After two months she was
sleeping through,

218
00:05:39,898 --> 00:05:41,638
and walking the dog again.

219
00:05:41,638 --> 00:05:42,930
And I watched her stop

220
00:05:42,930 --> 00:05:44,731
doing the parking-lot
math.

221
00:05:44,899 --> 00:05:46,063
She just parked and got

222
00:05:46,063 --> 00:05:47,386
out like anyone else.

223
00:05:47,574 --> 00:05:48,280
She's been using

224
00:05:48,280 --> 00:05:49,673
it for six months now.

225
00:05:50,100 --> 00:05:51,224
The tightness is gone.

226
00:05:51,224 --> 00:05:52,547
The two a.m. is gone.

227
00:05:52,904 --> 00:05:53,869
She went to every one

228
00:05:53,869 --> 00:05:55,828
of the grandkids' games
this spring.

229
00:05:55,828 --> 00:05:56,543
One time,

230
00:05:56,543 --> 00:05:58,086
unlimited sessions.

231
00:05:58,304 --> 00:06:00,303
Ten thousand people are
using it now.

232
00:06:00,541 --> 00:06:01,784
No prescription.

233
00:06:01,784 --> 00:06:02,868
No appointment.

234
00:06:02,868 --> 00:06:03,962
Nothing to book.

235
00:06:04,160 --> 00:06:05,533
Twenty minutes a day,

236
00:06:05,533 --> 00:06:06,428
and that's it.

237
00:06:06,676 --> 00:06:08,426
Right now it's 50 percent
off,

238
00:06:08,426 --> 00:06:10,355
which comes to under 80
dollars.

239
00:06:10,355 --> 00:06:12,305
Less than one visit to
that clinic.

240
00:06:12,543 --> 00:06:14,682
And it comes with a 90-day
guarantee.

241
00:06:14,900 --> 00:06:16,601
Use it daily for three
months,

242
00:06:16,769 --> 00:06:18,002
and if your knee isn't
better

243
00:06:18,002 --> 00:06:19,742
you get every penny back.

244
00:06:19,742 --> 00:06:20,965
No forms.

245
00:06:20,965 --> 00:06:21,970
No questions.

246
00:06:21,970 --> 00:06:23,273
You don't even send it
back.

247
00:06:23,431 --> 00:06:25,103
So here's where you
actually are.

248
00:06:25,420 --> 00:06:27,221
You can keep waiting to
feel better,

249
00:06:27,498 --> 00:06:28,433
with a real chance

250
00:06:28,433 --> 00:06:29,816
you simply never do.

251
00:06:30,223 --> 00:06:31,327
Or you can spend a few

252
00:06:31,327 --> 00:06:32,480
weeks calming the tissue

253
00:06:32,480 --> 00:06:33,713
that has been swollen
since

254
00:06:33,713 --> 00:06:35,066
the day they closed you
up.

255
00:06:35,384 --> 00:06:36,547
Because nobody is going

256
00:06:36,547 --> 00:06:37,810
to call you about this.

257
00:06:37,810 --> 00:06:39,889
That appointment already
ended.

258
00:06:40,077 --> 00:06:41,101
It ended the day

259
00:06:41,101 --> 00:06:42,634
the X-ray came back fine.

260
00:06:42,792 --> 00:06:43,906
You have to go looking.

261
00:06:43,906 --> 00:06:47,436
P.S. Don't stop anything
your doctor

262
00:06:47,436 --> 00:06:48,738
has you on, and don't

263
00:06:48,738 --> 00:06:50,280
cancel anything on your
own.

264
00:06:50,488 --> 00:06:52,040
Use the wrap a few weeks,

265
00:06:52,040 --> 00:06:53,322
see what the knee does,

266
00:06:53,322 --> 00:06:54,466
then go from there.

267
00:06:54,466 --> 00:06:56,426
The point isn't to fight
your doctor.

268
00:06:56,823 --> 00:06:58,215
It's to treat the one
thing

269
00:06:58,215 --> 00:07:00,581
the prescription pad and
the operating room

270
00:07:00,581 --> 00:07:02,232
were never built to reach.

271
00:07:02,232 --> 00:07:05,335
P.P.S. The guarantee
covers the whole window.

272
00:07:05,692 --> 00:07:07,363
Most people notice the
change somewhere

273
00:07:07,363 --> 00:07:08,785
in weeks two to four,

274
00:07:08,785 --> 00:07:09,759
and it keeps building

275
00:07:09,759 --> 00:07:11,272
from there with daily use.

276
00:07:11,649 --> 00:07:13,339
If it doesn't work you
keep

277
00:07:13,339 --> 00:07:15,001
it and they still refund
you.

278
00:07:15,378 --> 00:07:16,362
The only thing you risk

279
00:07:16,362 --> 00:07:17,148
is the time.

280
00:07:17,446 --> 00:07:20,767
P.P.P.S. If somebody else
in your house

281
00:07:20,767 --> 00:07:22,011
is living the same way,

282
00:07:22,179 --> 00:07:23,124
